---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Accessibility"
  description="The accessibility statement for ui.half-built-robots.com: conformance status, known limitations, and how to report a barrier."
>
  <main>
    <article class="static-page bracket-frame">
      <h1>Accessibility</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This is an accessibility statement from Curt Henrichs LLC for
          ui.half-built-robots.com, the reference site for the @half-built
          packages.
        </p>

        <h2>Conformance status</h2>
        <p>
          The
          <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/standards-guidelines/wcag/"
            >Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG)</a
          >
          define requirements for making web content accessible to people with
          disabilities. This site is partially conformant with WCAG 2.2 Level
          AA. Partially conformant means that some parts of the content do not
          fully conform to the standard.
        </p>

        <h2>Feedback</h2>
        <p>
          Report an accessibility barrier on this site through any of these:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Email:
            <a href="mailto:curthenrichs@gmail.com">curthenrichs@gmail.com</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            X/Twitter: <a href="https://x.com/curt_henrichs">@curt_henrichs</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            Bluesky:
            <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/curt-henrichs.bsky.social"
              >@curt-henrichs.bsky.social</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            GitHub:
            <a href="https://github.com/curthenrichs/half-built-ui/issues"
              >open an issue</a
            >
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Technical specifications</h2>
        <p>
          The site relies on HTML, CSS, and JavaScript working with the browser
          and any assistive technology in use.
        </p>

        <h2>Known limitations</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>
            The palette editor accepts any base colors. The shipped palette is
            what the automated checks test, and a custom palette can fall below
            the contrast requirements. The editor shows the contrast ratios of
            the current palette next to the controls, and its reset button
            restores the shipped colors.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>Please report any issue not listed here.</p>

        <h2>Assessment approach</h2>
        <p>
          Curt Henrichs assessed this site by self-evaluation. Every change to
          the site also runs an automated check (axe-core) against the level
          above, on every page in both the light and dark themes and with the
          interactive demos opened.
        </p>

        <h2>Date</h2>
        <p>This statement was written on September 29, 2026.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>
